# argument/ — schema

One result, one registry shard, per file (CLAUDE.md L4). `rk check`'s linker gate
(docs/gate-contracts.md Gate 2) enforces this file format and the module graph it describes; a
violation is an ERROR or WARN reported by `rk check`, not a style preference. Shards may live
anywhere under `argument/`, at any depth — the gate discovers `argument/**/*.md`, RECURSIVE,
excluding only files whose basename is exactly `README.md`, `INDEX.md`, or `DAG.md` at any depth.
`argument/lemmas/` is a common convention for grouping shards, not a requirement; a shard directly
at `argument/lem-foo.md` is exactly as valid as one nested under `argument/lemmas/lem-foo.md`.

**`argument/INDEX.md`/`DAG.md` (optional, generated, never hand-edited).** Neither file is
stamped by `rk init` — adoption is manual. To adopt: generate the two files once, then declare
them in `.rk/generated.json` (not stamped either; create it yourself):
```json
{ "schema_version": "1", "entries": [
  { "path": "argument/INDEX.md", "generator": "linker-index" },
  { "path": "argument/DAG.md", "generator": "linker-dag" }
] }
```
Once declared, `rk check`'s freshness gate regenerates and byte-diffs both on every run — a
hand-edit or a stale copy is an ERROR, an absent declared file is an ERROR, and the whole
mechanism is silently skipped (never a finding) only when `.rk/generated.json` itself does not
exist. A campaign that never adopts either file is not penalized for it.

## Frontmatter

Flat `key: value` lines between two `---` lines, at the top of the file.

| field | required | allowed values |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | yes | must equal the filename stem; convention `lem-`\|`thm-`\|`prop-`\|`cor-`\|`op-`\|`obs-<slug>` (not machine-enforced beyond the stem match) |
| `kind` | yes | one of `lemma`, `proposition`, `theorem`, `corollary`, `open-problem`, `obstruction` |
| `contract` | by convention (not required-field-checked) | one-line canonical statement; the anti-drift invariant against the af root conjecture |
| `defs` | no | list of `definitions/` ids this shard depends on — single-line `;`-list, or multi-line YAML list (one id per `- ` item) |
| `deps` | no | list of registry ids that are unconditional prerequisites (DAG edges) — single-line `;`-list, or multi-line YAML list (one id per `- ` item) |
| `routes` | no | OPTIONAL grouped-OR prerequisite sets — single-line grammar `[a; b] \| [c]` (each bracketed group is one route, a conjunction of its members; groups separated by `\|`), or the equivalent multi-line YAML list (one bracketed route group per `- ` item); any one route suffices; absent means `[]` |
| `status` | no | one of `proved`, `cited`, `consensus`, `open`, `obstruction`, `disproved`, `stated`, `proved-mod-audit`, `conjecture`, `heuristic`, `numerical` |
| `af` | no, defaults `none` | one of `none`, `seeded`, `validated` |
| `provenance` | no | freeform; not parsed by this gate (see the provenance gate) |
| `owner` | no | freeform; not validated |
| `workspace` | no, but load-bearing when `af != none` | `proofs/<id>` path — required for the orphan/contract/brittleness checks to find the af workspace |

Rules the gate enforces: the dependency graph (`deps` union every `routes` member) must be
acyclic; every `dep`/`routes` member must resolve to a known registry id, and every `defs` member
to a known `definitions/` id; `af: validated` requires every unconditional `dep` to be available
(`af: validated` or `status: cited`) and, if `routes` is present, at least one full route
available; a workspace whose node count exceeds the brittleness soft cap (`.rk/config`'s
`linkerBrittlenessSoftCap`) WARNs — never blocks — to factor the tree into sub-lemmas.

`defs`, `deps`, and `routes` each accept two equivalent forms — pick whichever reads better for the
shard at hand, both parse to the same list:

```
deps: lem-a; lem-b
```

or

```
deps:
  - lem-a
  - lem-b
```

`routes`'s multi-line form takes one bracketed route group per `- ` item, e.g. `routes: [a; b] | [c]`
is equivalent to:

```
routes:
  - [a; b]
  - [c]
```

## Example — a complete minimal shard

A file named `lem-widget-bound.md`:

```markdown
---
id: lem-widget-bound
kind: lemma
contract: every widget's gadget-count is bounded by its weight.
defs: def-widget
deps:
status: conjecture
af: none
---

Statement and (eventually) proof sketch go here, after the frontmatter's closing `---`.
```

A shard ready for `af` validation additionally needs `workspace:` — e.g. replacing the last two
frontmatter lines above with:

```
status: proved
af: validated
workspace: proofs/lem-widget-bound
```
